<title>USA: ECI Telecom gets orders worth $20 mln.</title>
<headline>ECI Telecom gets orders worth $20 mln.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>ECI Telecom Ltd said Tuesday that it had received two orders from China, totaling $11 million and one from Brazil for $8.9 million.</p>
<p>The Israeli-based manufacturer of digital telecommunications and data transmission systems said the Chinese customers,  China Telecom and the Ministry of Post and Telecommunication, will use its equipment to expand domestic satellite earth station networks.</p>
<p>The Brazilian order, from  Embratel, is for domestic use of its equipment over fiber optic cable lines, the company said.</p>
</text>
